@andyross - Now I am really seeing why we need that z_sched_switch_spin()--if the ISR on CPUx exits before the aborted thread finishes switching out on CPUy then the thread on CPUx can corrupt that thread by re-creating it at thread level.

Something like ...
```
some k_timer_func() /* runs on CPUx */
{
k_thread_abort(some_thread);   /* something took too long. kill thread */
k_sem_give(some_sem);   /* restart the thread */
}

thread_entry()
{
    while (1) {
        k_thread_create(some_thread, ....);  /* some_thread runs on CPUy */
        k_sem_take(some_sem, WAIT_FOREVER);
    }
}

```

So yes, I see that we still need something like z_sched_switch_spin(), but somewhere else.
